                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 68.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Law XL of 1879.—The Hungarian Criminal Law as to
                        Offences.</hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Part II.—KINDS OF OFFENCES AND THE PENALTIES
                        THEREFOR.</hi>
                </p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapter I</hi>.—<hi rendition="#italic">Offences
                        against the state.</hi></p>
                <p>Paragraph 37. Not more than two months’ arrest and not more than 300 florins fine
                    shall be inflicted upon anyone who defiles, damages, or tears down the coat of
                    arms or the flag of this country, of the allied countries (Croatia-Slavonia), or
                    of the Austro-Hungarian Monarchy when publicly displayed; likewise upon anyone
                    who, with intent to insult, defiles, damages, or tears down the flag or coat of
                    arms publicly used as the insignia by either civil or military authorities.</p>
            </div>
